Your proposed plan is good, but before implementing it I want to improve the architecture so that the JWT implementation is production-quality and scalable for the entire LMS microservices project.

Please modify the implementation according to the following requirements.

===========================================================
GENERAL REQUIREMENTS
===========================================================

Analyze the existing auth-service completely before making any changes.

Do NOT regenerate the project.

Do NOT rewrite unrelated code.

Modify ONLY auth-service.

Keep the existing architecture and coding standards.

===========================================================
JWT LIBRARY
===========================================================

Use the latest stable JJWT version compatible with Spring Boot 3.x.

Do not use outdated versions if a newer compatible version exists.

===========================================================
JWT CLAIMS
===========================================================

Do NOT use email as the JWT subject.

Use the authenticated user's UUID as the JWT subject.

JWT should contain the following claims:

sub = userId (UUID)

email

role

authorities

tokenVersion

issuedAt

expiration

issuer

Generate the authorities in Spring Security format.

Examples

ROLE_STUDENT

ROLE_INSTRUCTOR

ROLE_ADMIN

===========================================================
TOKEN CONFIGURATION
===========================================================

Read all JWT configuration from application.properties.

jwt.secret

jwt.expiration

jwt.issuer

Do not hardcode secrets.

===========================================================
AUTHENTICATION
===========================================================

Keep BCrypt password encoding.

Convert the application to Stateless Authentication.

Remove HttpSession usage.

Configure Spring Security correctly.

Implement JwtAuthenticationFilter.

Implement JwtAuthenticationEntryPoint.

Populate SecurityContext from JWT.

===========================================================
LOGIN RESPONSE
===========================================================

Instead of modifying the existing AuthResponse, create a dedicated LoginResponse DTO.

The login response should contain

accessToken

tokenType

expiresIn

userId

email

role

===========================================================
REGISTER
===========================================================

Registration should remain unchanged.

Default role must remain

STUDENT

Do not allow users to register as ADMIN or INSTRUCTOR.

===========================================================
LOGOUT
===========================================================

For now implement stateless logout.

Logout should simply instruct the client to remove the access token.

Do NOT implement token blacklist yet.

===========================================================
REFRESH TOKEN
===========================================================

Do NOT implement refresh tokens yet.

However,

prepare the architecture for future refresh token support.

Design the code so RefreshTokenService can be added later without major refactoring.

===========================================================
SWAGGER
===========================================================

Configure Swagger to support JWT Bearer Authentication.

The Authorize button should work correctly.

Authenticated APIs should be testable directly from Swagger.

